xt"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"maxIterations","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for 20,000 +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"20√n.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Return Value","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization and locking on −A, from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fixed start vector; once k pairs are found, a run on the complement of their vectors checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that no copy of a multiple eigenvalue was missed. A Ritz pair is accepted when its residual","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · max(|λ|, s\/1000), s Gershgorin’s bound on the spectrum; the vectors","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, whose values are returned. The dense solver below 64","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, or when k is a third of them or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"smallest","type":